&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dein Rolle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Wir suchen eine &lt;strong&gt;Senior Procurement Operations Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, der/die unsere Procurement-Operations-Funktion verantwortet und sicherstellt, dass unsere Supply Chain effizient, skalierbar und wirtschaftlich erfolgreich aufgestellt ist.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;In dieser Rolle übernimmst du die Verantwortung für den &lt;strong&gt;gesamten Procurement-Operations-Prozess&lt;/strong&gt; – von der Beschaffung und Lieferantensteuerung über das Bestandsmanagement bis hin zur kontinuierlichen Optimierung unserer Systeme und Prozesse. Dabei stellst du sicher, dass unsere Produktion zuverlässig und reibungslos mit den benötigten Zutaten und Verpackungsmaterialien versorgt wird.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Du arbeitest eng mit den Bereichen &lt;strong&gt;Planning, Production, Finance, Culinary und Operations&lt;/strong&gt; zusammen und leistest einen wichtigen Beitrag dazu, dass die richtigen Produkte zur richtigen Zeit verfügbar sind. Gleichzeitig treibst du operative Exzellenz voran und unterstützt das weitere Wachstum von Factor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Deine Aufgaben&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du &lt;strong&gt;führst und entwickelst unser Procurement-Operations-Team&lt;/strong&gt; und verantwortest Einkauf, Lieferantenkoordination, Bestandsmanagement und Abfallreduzierung.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du steuerst den &lt;strong&gt;gesamten Procurement-Operations-Prozess&lt;/strong&gt; und stellst die zuverlässige Versorgung unserer Produktion mit Zutaten und Verpackungsmaterialien sicher (OTIFQ).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du verantwortest die &lt;strong&gt;Bestandssteuerung&lt;/strong&gt;, optimierst Produktverfügbarkeit und minimierst gleichzeitig Verschwendung sowie Bestandsrisiken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du treibst unsere &lt;strong&gt;Zero-Waste-Strategie&lt;/strong&gt; sowie die kontinuierliche Optimierung von Einkaufs-, Bestands- und Forecasting-Prozessen voran.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du arbeitest eng mit &lt;strong&gt;Planning, Finance, Supply Chain, Culinary und Production&lt;/strong&gt; zusammen, um Einkaufsstrategien und operative Abläufe zu optimieren.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du analysierst &lt;strong&gt;Procurement-KPIs und Einkaufsdaten&lt;/strong&gt;, entwickelst aussagekräftige Reports und Dashboards und leitest daraus Verbesserungsmaßnahmen ab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du identifizierst Möglichkeiten zur &lt;strong&gt;Automatisierung, Standardisierung und kontinuierlichen Verbesserung&lt;/strong&gt; unserer Procurement- und Inventory-Prozesse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Das bringst du mit&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5–6 Jahre relevante Berufserfahrung&lt;/strong&gt; in Supply Chain, Operations, Procurement oder Production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eine &lt;strong&gt;hands-on, proaktive und lösungsorientierte Arbeitsweise&lt;/strong&gt; sowie hohe Stressresistenz.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ein &lt;strong&gt;datengetriebenes und ergebnisorientiertes Mindset&lt;/strong&gt; mit einem ausgeprägten Interesse an Prozessoptimierung.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sehr gute &lt;strong&gt;Kommunikations- und Kollaborationsfähigkeiten&lt;/strong&gt; im Umgang mit unterschiedlichen Teams und Kulturen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fließende Englisch- und Deutschkenntnisse.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibilität für &lt;strong&gt;gelegentliche Wochenendarbeit und Dienstreisen&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Das bieten wir dir&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gestaltungsfreiheit:&lt;/strong&gt; Du hast die Freiheit, eigene Ideen einzubringen, voranzutreiben und umzusetzen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lernen &amp;amp; Entwicklung:&lt;/strong&gt; Dich erwarten zahlreiche Möglichkeiten zur fachlichen und persönlichen Weiterentwicklung.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Urlaub:&lt;/strong&gt; 24 Urlaubstage pro Jahr bei einer 40-Stunden-Woche, anteilig bei Teilzeit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrides Arbeiten:&lt;/strong&gt; Ein hybrides Arbeitsmodell mit durchschnittlich etwa &lt;strong&gt;2 Tagen pro Woche in unserem Büro in Amsterdam&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fahrtkostenerstattung:&lt;/strong&gt; Wir übernehmen die Kosten für deine Fahrten ins Büro.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sport &amp;amp; Fitness:&lt;/strong&gt; Du erhältst einen Rabatt auf deine ClassPass-Mitgliedschaft sowie auf deine Fitnessstudio-Mitgliedschaft über Bedrijfsfitness Nederland.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zusatzversicherung:&lt;/strong&gt; Profitiere von einem Rabatt auf deine zusätzliche Krankenversicherung bei Zilveren Kruis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Factor &amp;amp; HelloFresh:&lt;/strong&gt; Du erhältst einen Rabatt auf deine wöchentliche Factor-, HelloFresh- und/oder Green Chef-Box in den Niederlanden.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verpflegung im Büro:&lt;/strong&gt; Freue dich auf gesunde Mittagessen, Obst und Snacks in unserem Büro.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vergütung &amp;amp; Altersvorsorge:&lt;/strong&gt; Dich erwarten ein wettbewerbsfähiges Gehalt und ein attraktives Pensionsmodell.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team &amp;amp; Kultur:&lt;/strong&gt; Erlebe regelmäßige soziale Aktivitäten mit unserem kulturell vielfältigen und internationalen Team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are you up for the challenge?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Dann freuen wir uns auf deine vollständige Bewerbung. Bitte gib dabei auch deine &lt;strong&gt;Gehaltsvorstellung und deinen frühestmöglichen Eintrittstermin&lt;/strong&gt; an.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;FEQ427R334&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are on a mission to empower our customers to solve the world&#39;s toughest data problems by utilizing the the Databricks Data Intelligence Platform. As a Delivery Solutions Architect (DSA), you will play an important role during this journey. You will collaborate with our sales and field engineering teams to accelerate the adoption and growth of the Databricks platform in your customers. You will also help ensure customer success by increasing focus and technical accountability to our most complex customers who need guidance to accelerate usage on Databricks workloads that they have already selected, helping them maximise the value they get of our platform and the return on investment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid technical and commercial role. It is commercial in the sense that you will drive growth in your assigned customers and use cases through leading your customers&#39; stakeholders, building executive relationships, orchestration of other focused/specialized teams within Databricks, and creating and driving plans and strategies for Databricks colleagues to build upon. This is in parallel to being technical, with expectations being that you become the post-sale technical lead across all Databricks products. This requires you to use your skills and technical credibility to engage and communicate at all levels with an organisation. You will report directly to a DSA Manager within the Field Engineering organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Solutions Architects to understand the full use case demand plan for prioritised customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the post-technical win technical account strategy and execution plan for the majority of Databricks use cases within our most strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the accountable technical leader assigned to specific use cases and customer(s) across multiple selling teams and internal stakeholders, creating certainty from uncertainty and driving onboarding, enablement, success, go-live and healthy consumption of the workloads where the customer has made the decision to consume Databricks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the first contact for any technical issues or questions related to production/go live status of agreed upon use cases within an account, oftentimes services multiple use cases within the largest and most complex organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage both Shared Services, User Education, Onboarding/Technical Services and Support resources, along with escalating to expert level technical experts to build the right tasks that are beyond your scope of activities or expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, own and execute a point-of-view as to how key use cases can be accelerated into production, coordinating with Professional Services (PS) resources on the delivery of PS Engagement proposals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate Databricks Product and Engineering teams for new product Innovations, private previews and upgrade needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop an execution plan that covers all activities of all customer-facing technical roles and teams to cover the below work streams:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Main use cases moving from ‘win’ to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enablement / user growth plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product adoption (strategy and activities to increase adoption of Databricks’ Lakehouse vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organic needs for current investment (e.g. cloud cost control, tuning &amp;amp; optimization)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive and operational governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide internal and external updates - KPI reporting on the status of usage and customer health, covering investment status, important risks, product adoption and use case progression - to your Technical GM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience where you have been accountable for technical project / program delivery within the domain of Data and AI and where you can contribute to technical debate and design choices with customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience in Python, SQL or Scala&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a customer-facing pre-sales, technical architecture, customer success, or consulting role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of solution architecture related distributed data systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how to attribute business value and outcomes to specific project deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical program, or project management including account, stakeholder and resource management accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience resolving complex and important escalation with senior customer executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting open-ended discovery workshops,&amp;nbsp; creating strategic roadmaps, conducting business analysis and managing delivery of complex programmes/projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of overachievement against quota, Goals or similar objective targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, or equivalent experience through work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in French and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can travel up to 30% when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP Media&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships – all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open – we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is WPP&#39;s AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;wppmedia.com&quot;&gt;wppmedia.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3617 - Associate Director, Implementational Planning, UK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary and Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you looking to join a high-performance experienced team, whose ambition is to be the most distinctive and admired data driven, Digital Planning team in the UK?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is your opportunity to accelerate our clients digital and data transformation strategy whilst developing our Digital Planning IP within Wavemaker.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will suit candidates with deep digital or performance marketing expertise, with a strong track record of quality and innovation in implementational planning or activation. The role is stretching, giving candidates responsibility for the advancement of a client group’s whole Digital marketing output and the fitness of our operating model to deliver this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Digital Planning Lead to audit our clients digital maturity, through the WM-Operating System and Digital Maturity Framework, delivering a set of indicators and actions, that drive growth and ensure our clients are future-fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with the digital planning lead and Nexus activation teams, support in the leadership of the overall digital channel investment and ensure WM commercial considerations are taken into account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Wavemaker product owners and with Data Partners, to ensure the right capabilities and technology are in place on the account to advance Digital marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Data &amp;amp; Tech teams, as well as identify new opportunities to advance our clients through the suite of Digital Analytics solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work ‘upstream’ with Strategy &amp;amp; Planning to ensure outputs from Provocative Planning are translated into credible Digital marketing approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work ‘downstream’ with Platform Leads and Nexus Activation teams to ensure that the Digital channel approaches are activated with rigour and innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the digital lead in ensuring that all Digital channels are fully integrated into weekly/monthly client updates and meetings (this includes Ecommerce, Affiliates, and OneSearch : PPC &amp;amp; SEO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support a ‘fluid’ way of working with Platform activation resource within each client hub.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being accountable to the Digital Planning Lead and Digital Planning Partner for the timely, high-quality delivery of digital marketing on the account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support on new business pitches and help bring the strongest Digital solutions to our pitch RFI, RFP and presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client Partnering and Consulting with Agency knowledge.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responds to key Digital stakeholder requests in an accurate, timely and professional manner and seeks to have a good understanding of client needs and challenges. Gains stakeholder trust by responding to stakeholder requests and needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a good understanding of how the agency operates and works with their clients. Knows about the clients’ business and who the key digital decision-makers are there.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital Channel Strategic thinking and Planning
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates an interest in client challenges by asking relevant questions and helps to gather insights to help aid digital planning. Follows instructions to meet client needs but is prepared and confident to challenge briefs. Builds digital case studies and gathers insights on clients to support the team and share learnings. Demonstrates understanding of digital campaign optimization strategies and how to meet key performance indicators. Uses big picture and critical thinking in day-to-day role, flagging and escalating potential issues in client work to team members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Knowledge of Products and Technical Communication skills
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a good understanding of Xaxis, Nexus and Finecast product and service offerings and across all digital channels. Can discuss all digital channels, products and opportunities with confidence and can apply this knowledge to meet client/agency needs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Acumen
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a clear understanding of how finance works and how the agency makes a profit. Ensures exceptional finance management for digital clients and works with Nexus activation teams to ensure the finance process is adhered to, including any required booking, reconciling and documenting activity within deadline (including timesheets) and addressing finance queries. Demonstrates a growing understanding of the financial impact of decisions/solutions to drive projects and analyses that support the agencies mission. Understands GroupM’s trading strategies and processes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital Industry Knowledge
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates basic understanding themes in the Digital industry (programmatic/Paid Search/ SEO/AI/digital media/platforms/Analytics). Research industry information and summarizes findings. Recognizes different digital products and services and begins to understand how they are applied.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideas Creation
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates curiosity by asking questions regarding current products/services and processes. Contributes to idea generation within team settings. Provides ideas and new solutions, methods and products to update what existed prior. Demonstrates willingness to try new and innovative ideas, products and solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Life at WPP Media &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Our passion for shaping the next era of media is powered by our commitment to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Be Extraordinary, investing in our employees to inspire transformational creativity. We also&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Lead Optimistically, firmly believing in and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Championing Growth and Development&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;for every individual. This commitment allows WPP Media employees to leverage the extensive global WPP Media &amp;amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, build vital professional connections, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Create an Open environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;built on trust and respect, where everyone feels they belong and has opportunities to progress. This inclusive culture is fostered through a variety of employee resource groups and frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our comprehensive benefits package reflects this commitment, including competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental health awareness days.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;WPP Media is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to characteristics. We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection in this open and supportive environment. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;  Please note that while our philosophy is the same across WPP, benefits may vary by office/country.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Please note this is a UK based role and requires individuals to have the right to work in this location&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Please read our Privacy Notice (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; for more information on how we process the information you provide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:276}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
